From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:59:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a function entry an autoload replaces alive while it is
 bound

Binding a function's arguments can autoload an extension that adds
overloads to that very function, as `epoch(TIMESTAMPTZ) + 2.5` does
with icu: the binder looks up `+`, binds `epoch(...)`, whose
placeholder loads icu, and icu's ALTER_ON_CONFLICT replaces `+`, `-`
and `age` outside a transaction. CatalogSet::AlterEntry destroyed the
replaced entry at once, so the binder chose an overload from freed
memory: `+` computed `-`, `-` bound as `age`, or the process crashed.

A non-transactional alter of the system catalog now keeps the replaced
version as the child of the new one, where lookups never reach it,
and FunctionBinder::GetCurrentEntry looks an entry that has been
replaced up again in its own schema before an overload is chosen,
for scalar, aggregate, window, table and recursive-CTE USING KEY
binding.

Carried here until upstream takes it; upstream's attempt is
duckdb/duckdb#27950, not merged. duckdb/duckdb-r#2883.
---
 src/duckdb/src/catalog/catalog_set.cpp        |  8 ++++++-
 src/duckdb/src/function/function_binder.cpp   | 24 ++++++++++++++++---
 .../duckdb/function/function_binder.hpp       |  5 ++++
 .../query_node/bind_recursive_cte_node.cpp    |  3 ++-
 .../binder/tableref/bind_table_function.cpp   |  7 +++---
 5 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/catalog/catalog_set.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/catalog/catalog_set.cpp
index 44c9bb700..feca6586b 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/catalog/catalog_set.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/catalog/catalog_set.cpp
@@ -385,11 +385,17 @@ bool CatalogSet::AlterEntry(CatalogTransaction transaction, const Identifier &na
 
 		DuckTransactionManager::Get(GetCatalog().GetAttached())
 		    .PushCatalogEntry(*transaction.transaction, new_entry->Child(), stream.GetData(), stream.GetPosition());
-	} else {
+	} else if (!catalog.IsSystemCatalog()) {
 		// if we don't have a transaction this alter is non-transactional
 		// in that case we are able to just directly destroy the child (if there is any)
 		entry_to_destroy = new_entry->TakeChild();
 	}
+	// A non-transactional alter of the system catalog (an extension adding overloads to a function it shares with
+	// core, e.g. while autoloading) keeps the replaced version as the child of the new one instead of destroying it.
+	// Clients hold system entries without a transaction pinning them, across work that can load an extension: binding
+	// a function's arguments, or a LOAD on another connection. Lookups never reach the retained version. It costs one
+	// copy of the function set per such alter, bounded because each extension loads once, and lives until shutdown
+	// (a DROP's tombstone keeps it too).
 
 	// Update shared entry state only after the alter is installed and rollbackable.
 	if (new_entry->name != entry->name) {
